    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the unequivocal engine of our offense. With an elite efficiency score of 85.94, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against Littell, and while the opposing battery presents a minor threat to stolen base upside, the positional advantage of the #2 spot in the order maximizes his run-scoring potential. Similarly, **Brice Turang** and **Josh Naylor** anchor the core with scores of 75.06 and 76.52, respectively; both players are seeing significant value boosts from favorable platoon dynamics and soft matchups against Agnos and Montero. **James Wood** remains a high-floor play despite facing the southpaw Rodriguez, as his elite xwOBA of .401 provides the cushion necessary to override the neutral platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was leaving **Austin Riley** on the bench. Despite a solid performance profile, his 46.15 score fell just short of our daily threshold due to a challenging date with Ashcraft, whose skill profile dragged down the overall efficiency rating. We opted to prioritize **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Tyler Soderstrom**, whose park factors and platoon alignments yielded higher projected output. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the bottom of our order; **Alex Freeland** is starting in the #9 hole, which dampens his total score, though his switch-hitting versatility keeps him marginally above the bench floor. \n\nRisk management remains paramount as we navigate the schedule. We have confirmed that **Mickey Moniak** remains unavailable due to his IL stint, and the weather-induced postponement of **Jose Caballero** has forced a static lineup adjustment. While we are confident in this configuration, owners should keep a close eye on the late-game defensive substitutions for **Dalton Rushing**, whose efficiency score is heavily weighted by the matchup against Kochanowicz; if the game turns into a blowout, his limited plate appearances could become a liability for our daily cap.",
